# Frontend

## Stack

- Templates: **EJS** under `views/` · Client JS/CSS under `public/`
- Bootstrap **5.3.8** CDN · shared theme in `/public/app.css` · no React/Tailwind
- Commit / push only when explicitly requested.

## Design system

- Tokens and admin utilities live in `/public/app.css` (linked from `common/header` after Bootstrap).
- Brand primary: `#5c8aa5` (maps to `--bs-primary`).
- Shared partials under `views/common/`:
  - `app-navbar` — admin top bar (use instead of copy-pasted nav)
  - `page-header` — breadcrumb + title + subtitle + actions
  - `page-alert` — `#…-alert` slot
  - `date-range` — from/to GET filter
  - `table-filters` — search + filter row
  - `list-table-shell` — card + empty/loading + table wrap
  - `icon-actions` — edit / delete / view SVG icon buttons (`.hb-icon-btn`)
  - `comments-panel` — detail-page comments
  - `form-modal` — standard modal chrome
- Page shells: `.hb-main` + `.hb-page` (standard) or `.hb-page-wide` (dense workflow lists).

## Page structure

- App pages use `<%- include('common/header') %>` and `<%- include('common/footer') %>`.
- Include `<%- include('common/app-navbar') %>` (pass `{ wide: true }` for fluid layout).
- Pass `title` and `username` from guarded UI routes; wire logout via `/public/app.js`.
- Always load `/public/utils.js` after `/public/app.js` and before the page script on app pages.
- Page-specific script: `/public/<page>.js` with `defer`.
- Date helpers: use `getWritableDate` / `getReadableDate` from `utils.js`. Prefer `data-readable-date` + `data-date-format`. Do not `slice` date strings.
- Confirm dialogs: `showConfirm({ title, description, choices })` — never `window.confirm`.
- Alerts: `showAlert(element, message, type)` / `hideAlert(element)` from `utils.js` — do not redefine locally.
- Prefer schema-first on the backend; implement UI only when asked.
- Flat paths: `/app/projects/:id`, `/app/invoices/:id`, etc.

## UX standards

- **Lists:** tables only for multi-record collections (dashboard/hub cards are nav-only exceptions).
- **Row navigation:** `data-href` on `<tr>` + `.hb-row-link`; `bindTableRowNavigation` runs globally from `utils.js`. Same-tab only (no `target="_blank"` for entity links).
- **Filters:** search on text lists; column sort via `th.hb-sortable` + `data-sort-key` / `bindSortableHeaders`; date-range via `common/date-range` when dates exist.
- **Actions:** edit/delete use `common/icon-actions` (same SVG buttons everywhere). Sentence case: `Add user`, `Save`, `Delete`.
- **Detail pages:** row click opens detail; collaboration detail pages use `common/comments-panel` labeled **Comments**.
- **Copy:** breadcrumbs `App / Section` or `App / Section / Record`; column headers consistent (`Created On`, `Due Date`).
- **Modals:** `h2.modal-title.h5`; Cancel `btn-outline-secondary`; Save `btn-primary`.

## UI patterns

- List page + Bootstrap modal for add when there is no separate create page.
- Forms: `novalidate`; client checks for UX; `fetch` JSON to `/api/…` with `credentials: "same-origin"`.
- On successful create/update/delete, `window.location.reload()` unless a sibling does otherwise.
- Missing entities → `/not-found`.

## Type casts

Skip fluff casts (`Boolean(query)`, `String(count)`, `typeof username !== "undefined"`). Prefer `query && …`, assign numbers directly to `textContent`, and `username || "user"` / `title || "HammerByte"` when locals are always passed from guarded routes.

**Keep** casts that prevent real breaks:

- `Number(...)` on DOM / `dataset` / form `.value` before JSON API payloads
- `Number(...).toFixed(2)` for DECIMAL money display in EJS and client JS
- `Number(query.month)` / `Number(query.year)` when reading query strings in UI routes

```js
// ❌ BAD
countElement.textContent = String(visibleRows.length);
row.classList.toggle("d-none", Boolean(query) && !haystack.includes(query));

// ✅ GOOD
countElement.textContent = visibleRows.length;
row.classList.toggle("d-none", query && !haystack.includes(query));
const payload = { id: Number(row.dataset.id), amount: Number(amountInput.value) };
```

## Helpers

- Shared UI helpers live in `/public/utils.js` (`showAlert`, `hideAlert`, `escapeHtml`, `bindTableRowNavigation`, `bindClientSearch`, `bindSortableHeaders`, `renderCommentItem`, dates, `showConfirm`, uploads).
- Do **not** extract a page-local helper for logic used in only one place — inline it. Extract only when the same block is used in two or more places in that file.
- Prefer object spread over rebuilding an object field-by-field.

## Naming

- Page script file name mirrors the view: `views/customers.ejs` → `public/customers.js`.
- DOM ids use kebab-case (`customer-form`, `invoice-items`).
- API JSON bodies use snake_case field names matching the backend.
- Never use short forms or cryptic abbreviations for variables or parameters — spell the word out:

```js
// ❌ BAD
const pl = { … };
const btn = document.getElementById("…");

// ✅ GOOD
const payload = { … };
const submitButton = document.getElementById("…");
```

  Also avoid truncations (`Btn` → `Button`, `El` → `Element`) and single/double-letter stand-ins. Prefer `catch (error)`.
